<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Orbulaq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1643</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakh-dzungar-wars">Kazakh–Dzungar wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Orbulaq was fought in 1643 in the mountains of Zhetysu in south-eastern Kazakhstan between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir-khan">Jahangir Khan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erdeni-batur">Erdeni Batur</a>. According to accounts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a>, with a small force of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a> in entrenchments in a mountain pass, held off a much larger Dzungar army until reinforcements under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yalangtush-bahadur">Yalangtush Bahadur</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> arrived. It is celebrated in Kazakhstan as a heroic defence.</p></div>
